  "description": "Vetoing sets the voter's standing vote on that movie to 'no' so the standing and round layers can never contradict each other",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Veto: 'Vetoing sets the voter's standing vote on that movie to no, so the two layers can never contradict each other.'",
  "rationale": "4 attendees, all rows present on all three movies. m1: 4 yes -> approval 1.00; m2: 3 yes (u1,u2,u3 yes; u4 no) -> approval 0.75; m3: 2 yes -> approval 0.50. All promoted, ranked m1, m2, m3. u3 - who currently holds a standing YES on m2 - vetoes m2. vetoes(m2) = 1 >= VETO_THRESHOLD 1 -> m2 disqualified; survivors {m1,m3} = 2, so the exception does not fire. Round robin over survivors: m1 vs m3 = 3 (u1,u2,u4) to 1 (u3) -> Condorcet winner m1. Required side effect: u3's StandingVote on m2 is upserted from yes to no. This is a forward-looking write - it does not retroactively change this round's tallies (m2 was tallied at 3 yes / approval 0.75) but next round m2 would tally 2 yes of 4 rows = approval 0.50.",
